---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Accessibility | Crossbell Vending"
  description="Crossbell Vending's commitment to an accessible website and how to report a barrier."
  heading="Accessibility"
  updated="2026-09-12"
>
  <p>
    {site.legalName} wants every visitor to be able to read this site and reach us, whatever
    device or assistive technology they use. We build to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines
    (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every page can be navigated by keyboard, with a visible focus indicator and a skip-to-content link.</li>
    <li>Headings, landmarks, and form labels are structured so screen readers announce them correctly.</li>
    <li>Text and background colors meet AA contrast ratios.</li>
    <li>Images carry descriptive alternative text; decorative images are hidden from assistive technology.</li>
    <li>The site respects your reduced-motion preference and works without JavaScript.</li>
    <li>Layouts adapt from phone screens to large monitors without horizontal scrolling.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tell us if something is in the way</h2>
  <p>
    If any part of this site is difficult to use, we want to fix it. Email
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or call
    <a href={`tel:${site.phoneTel}`}>{site.phone}</a> and tell us the page and what happened.
    We respond by the end of the business day.
  </p>

  <h2>Our coolers</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about the physical accessibility of a Crossbell cooler — reach height, clearance,
    or payment options — are welcome at the same contact details. We consider placement height
    and clear floor space during every site walkthrough.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
